the clark county fire department has  taken the lead on the investigation into  the explosion at a boulder city business  where six employees were injured in that  blast at arma rock palmeri country  concrete earlier this week we're told  the county's hazmat team has been there  to assess hazardous material at the  scene and employees say the facility is  closed for the time being now out of  those six employees injured one was  severely hurt by the blast that's right  and today for the first time victoria  saha spoke with that employee who  describes the destruction  the employee that was closest to the  blast had severe burns and was rushed to  umc trauma from his hospital bed he  tells me he was determined to live i was  standing there looking down on my arms  watching my skin melt  thirty-two-year-old eddie diganji  describes a normal working day quickly  turning into horror this is life or  death  that's that's the first thing i thought  and i said i'm not dying diganji was  working on his machine at the concrete  facility when suddenly i felt the  explosion i saw it in front of me  it blew me a few feet back  conscious the whole time he took off his  burning clothes and tried to find the  nearest exit where his wife nikki  diganji who works in the same facility  was frantically looking for him i heard  the explosion and it shook everything  and i heard  screaming  and i just told myself i i hope that's  not eddie i hope it's not him  and  as i listened i was like oh my god i  think it is colleagues started pouring  water all over the ganges as the  ambulance arrived i just wanted the  burning to stop once at the hospital he  was met by his distraught mom first  thing he said his mom quit being a  crybaby but it's hard just  picturing him you know in pain i i have  no idea  how i'm even alive right now it needs a  walking miracle diganji still has a long  road to recovery doctors believe he'll  be here at umc trauma for about a month  the family has set up a gofundme to help  with any expenses we have that link up  on our website at 8newsnow.com  victoria saha live local now
 

